     Monsters who attempt to carry the Amulet up stairs in Gehennom
are subject to a variation of the "mysterious force" which afflicts
your character when doing same, and will sometimes be level teleported
down one level instead of successfully climbing up.  So using a monster
to carry the Amulet for you would be pretty tedious.

     The mysterious force never kicks in on the bottom 2 or 3 levels,
so watching a monster carry the Amulet out of the sanctum level doesn't
provide enough feedback to gauge whether this would be useful.  There
does seem to be at least one advantage here though when the monster
is one who teleports to the stairs when wounded.  It can do that on
levels where you can't teleport, so then you could level teleport up
and come down the stairs, bypassing tedious traversal of the demon
lairs.  But overall I suspect that the amount of effort will work out
to be more than simply carrying the Amulet the ordinary way.


